  "id": "us11-console-observability-r1",
  "approval": "Human review ① 2026-10-21: user answered 「没问题，可以进入后续了」 after the R3 revision round and approved the US-11 module card for registration and downstream work. Reviewed path docs/us/us11-console-observability.md, sha256 f0c802a050a0dea98e5338d77292ec6c2f9aaceeebf90016a7cd912216ad56b3, 2464 lines (R3, 2026-10-21); registered by /us-register 11 (REGISTRY line 38). Frozen derived inputs: spec sha256 02acdfba8bb8b073f8d93d6e7b395345b197483e86ee9452cae1e762626b4d6b, plan sha256 a580421c1d2a2e5d15b9f53672dc2ad7de154a310d8832b45a8ccc08c2c1d3e5, tasks sha256 f01b2a0a0fad8b39ac1f72ca84b596220baabc3d6ee5f51c17828e80fc062799 (217 lines, 53 checked / 4 open at derivation, T052–T055; T056/T057 were already inside the frozen file). Stage derived from module card §4.4 by module-dev step 6.1: seventeen checks, required_tests expanded to exact names (no wildcards), tasks mapping limited to tasks whose tests a stage check actually executes. Race-name alignment to §4.4 on 2026-10-21, no assertion weakening: TestAgentEditor_UpdateContentConcurrentSavesExactlyOneWins renamed to TestAgentEditor_ConcurrentSave; TestWatcher_ConcurrentEvents added to internal/workspace/watcher_test.go. Recorded in run-state I-70. Additive criteria extension 2026-10-21 (T054 defect fixes, no assertion weakened): 011-app-baseline gains TestLoadProviderDefinitions_* / TestLoadMCPServerDefinitions_* (published definition block must be a mapping); 011-app-registry gains TestAgentProfilesPort_LiveRegistryMerge and TestRun_ServeStartsConfigWatcher (production watcher wiring + /profiles live registry per card constraints 28/39 and figure A ⑧–⑩). Fix round after human review ② 2026-10-21 (returned; not an approval): F1 narrows skill-version read allowance to the run-bound version directories per card line 610 / note 21, with contract §1.1 ToolEnv.SkillDirs added by that ruling; protect list gains internal/core/action.go and the two internal/tool constraint-31 test files, count corrected to 29 modified production / 14 modified test files. No assertion weakened, no required_tests removed. Additive criteria extension 2026-10-21 (review ② decisions #1 / #2 / #9; no assertion weakened, no required_tests removed, approved scope unchanged): 011-core-resources selector gains TestAgentService_Resources_ and requires the four pinned-client / admission-lease regressions; 011-workspace-lifecycle requires TestLifecycleStore_DiscardRollsBackCreationUnderCallerHeldLock (caller-held write-lock contract); 011-app-registry selector gains and requires TestRun_SnapshotUsesValidatedRegistryConfig and TestRun_SnapshotKeepsPublishedConfigAfterRejectedDiskEdit (defect-1 snapshot single source, both regressions required by decision #1); 011-app-runtime-admin requires TestRunResources_ProviderIsAuditedPinnedView and TestRunResources_ReadLockLeasesUntilReleaseAdmission. The 011-web-observability selector question stays open pending a human ruling. Input refresh and corrections 2026-10-21 after the independent review of the review ② fix round (findings F-02 / F-05 / F-06 / F-07 / F-08; not an approval): an earlier revision of this field stated the derivation-time task counts as 53 checked / 2 open with T056/T057 appended; that statement was wrong — the frozen pre-revision tasks.md (sha256 f01b2a0a0fad8b39ac1f72ca84b596220baabc3d6ee5f51c17828e80fc062799, 217 lines) held 53 checked / 4 open (T052–T055), and T056/T057 were already inside it. Current frozen inputs: module card docs/us/us11-console-observability.md sha256 d8b4c68e6e8fe34d5e2a41a6d6573d55824512057fdbefca202d2c95761e7854, 2524 lines (R3 plus review ② fix revisions; §3.6 corrected to plan 29 / actual 34 / +7 unlisted); spec sha256 327680f3c3ac28bfc4a084d3a997328607bb8d6151691a34df67aff6849c0542, 305 lines; plan sha256 3e0529fe26930571485eb325544f8ba5c5f2c8aca9e6e4d403eac5e49fc09045, 199 lines; tasks sha256 a115ef19b94e90611b6680d84e684a751f752fd8107a665960e18cd9e3de7c37, 217 lines, 57 checked / 0 open. Additive criteria extension of the same round, no assertion weakened and no required_tests removed: 011-web-content-lifecycle requires TestLifecycle_Enable_RequiresPublishedResources (enable re-checks published resources, finding F-02); 011-race additionally requires TestAgentService_Resources_ToolEnvCarriesBoundSkillDirs, TestReadFileTool_ReadsPublishedSkillVersionPaths, TestWriteFileTool_RefusesPublishedSkillVersionPaths, TestWhitelistPolicy_AllowsOnlyRunBoundSkillVersionReads, TestLifecycle_Enable_RequiresPublishedResources and TestProfiles_LifecycleAndRunnable (finding F-07). TestListDirTool_RefusesOutOfRootSymlinkTarget (finding F-05) is deliberately not a required_tests name because it skips on hosts without the symlink privilege; it executes in Linux CI. Open rulings still pending: F-01 (spec FR-019 / card constraint 17 prose vs figure F / constraint 46 on the Agent read-lock span), F-03 (runtime demotion when a bound skill loses its published version) and F-04 (whether the F1 narrowing also covers the .basalt/skills/ working copy). Console visual correction 2026-10-21 (not an approval; triggered by the user opening the running console and finding every page rendered with browser defaults): the console shipped without any stylesheet — main.ts imported none, dist/assets held only the script, and §3.1.25's deliverable tree listed no style file, so neither tasks nor criteria required one. Fix: assets/console/src/styles.css implements the approved style-A tokens (design review §4.2/§4.3) and is imported by main.ts; dist and integrity.json were rebuilt; the module card §3.1.25 now lists src/styles.css (current card sha256 4d3ffa8eb725082305289925ffd126e014862adf4a62e91037451520917e3496, 2526 lines; the hash recorded above is the pre-fix revision). No required_tests added or removed; TestConsole_StaticAssetCacheHeaders now asserts the .js and .css artifacts separately (additive — the existing JS assertion is unchanged, no assertion weakened). This stage text changed, so the stage must be re-run before any resubmission evidence; this stage grants no approval by itself. Five-ruling round 2026-10-22 (human decisions; F-01 A prose alignment, F-03 A registration filtering, F-04 B1 explicit run marker, INFO-1 US-12 obligation, INFO-2 A local contract note; not an approval): F-01 A rewrote spec FR-019 and card constraint 17 to the short Agent read lock plus ResourceGate lease, naming the state-release decision as the admission linearization point; no implementation change. F-03 A adds published-pointer filtering shared by startup and watcher (absent publication demotes at startup and retires via watcher with scheduler SetRegistered(false); pointer lookup failure fails startup closed and keeps the old registry in the watcher), with WARN carrying the fixed reason `skill version missing: <name>`; additive required_tests: 011-app-baseline gains TestRegistryEntries_SkillWithoutPublishedPointerIsNotRegistered and TestRegistryEntries_PointerLookupFailureRejectsStartup (selector gains TestRegistryEntries_), 011-app-registry gains TestRegistrySync_RetiresAgentWithoutPublishedSkill and TestRegistrySync_PointerLookupFailureKeepsOldRegistry. F-04 B1 threads ToolEnv.RunBound through Action into Policy so run-bound file reads refuse the .basalt/skills work copy even with no skill bound; additive 011-race required_tests TestFileTools_RunBoundRefusesSkillWorkCopy and TestWhitelistPolicy_RefusesSkillWorkCopyReadInsideRun. INFO-2 A adds only a local description on AgentFilesView.lifecycle in openapi.yaml (field shape unchanged). DEMO-INFO-1 adds a data-URI SVG icon link to assets/console/index.html and rebuilds dist plus integrity.json (three artifacts). No assertion weakened and no required_tests removed. Current frozen input hashes are recorded in run-state; this stage text changed, so it must be re-run before resubmission evidence; this stage grants no approval by itself. Additive criteria extension 2026-10-22 after the independent review of the closeout round (finding R-03; not an approval): 011-web-content-lifecycle selector gains TestConsoleDist_ and requires TestConsoleDist_IntegrityMatchesFiles, TestConsoleDist_NoExternalReferences and TestConsoleDist_NoStrayFiles, so embed-integrity regressions are caught by the dedicated check rather than only by make check and CI; 011-app-baseline requires TestRegistryEntries_MultipleMissingSkillsSortedJoin, pinning the agent-md.md rule 5 literal for multiple missing skills (ascending, comma+space) and the R-04 disposition; no assertion weakened and no required_tests removed. This stage text changed, so it must be re-run before resubmission evidence; this stage grants no approval by itself.",
